# The rover tree ends up on a Linux rootfs. Force LF in the working tree.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# ====================
# fpms-os/.gitattributes has carried this rule for a while, but it only governs
# fpms-os/. The rover source -- the .py files, stack/, nav2/, slam/ -- sits two
# levels ABOVE it and was covered by nothing, so on a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true every one of those files lands CRLF. Measured: all 38
# payload files.
#
# `git ls-files --eol` showed `i/lf w/crlf attr/` -- the committed content was
# always fine, so this is not a repository corruption. It is a working-tree
# problem, and the working tree is exactly what the image build reads.
#
# WHAT IT COSTS WHEN IT IS WRONG
# ==============================
#   stack/fpms-uros-supervisor gets a shebang ending "\r", and
#   fpms-uros-supervisor.service ExecStart=s that path directly, so exec fails:
#
#       /usr/local/bin/fpms-uros-supervisor: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter:
#       No such file or directory
#
#   which is spectacularly misleading -- /usr/bin/env plainly exists and the
#   file looks perfect in every editor. That unit supervises the micro-ROS
#   drive link, so the symptom is a rover that cannot move.
#
#   nav2/arena_map.yaml stays CRLF, so the image build's comparison against a
#   freshly generated (LF) map can never match on a text diff -- which failed
#   the build for a completely spurious reason.
#
#   Every ~/*.py is installed 0755 with a \r shebang: fine under the units
#   (which run `python3 file.py`) and broken the moment anyone runs ./file.py.
#
# The image build normalises the payload defensively at stage 30, but that
# repairs a copy. This repairs the source, which is where it should be fixed.
#
# NOTE: applying this renormalises the working tree on the next checkout. The
# committed bytes do not change -- they were already LF.
*               text eol=lf

# Binary payloads that must never be touched.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.pgm           binary
*.rknn          binary
*.onnx          binary
*.pt            binary
*.bin           binary
*.img           binary
*.tar.gz        binary
*.posegraph     binary
